  "answer_text": "It looks like you're referring to **Iuka, Mississippi** (sometimes spelled \"Luka\"). Here's what we know about it:\n\n- Iuka is a city in and the county seat of **Tishomingo County, Mississippi**, United States.\n\n- Its population was **3,139** at the 2020 census.\n\n- **Woodall Mountain**, the highest point in Mississippi, is located just south of Iuka.\n\n- Iuka is built on the site of a **Chickasaw village**, and the name \"Iuka\" comes from the name of one of the chiefs of the village.\n\n- Iuka was founded by **David Hubbard**, a wagon train scout, and Euro-American settlers arrived with the Memphis and Charleston Railroad in **1857**.\n\n- The **Civil War** brought widespread devastation when a major engagement occurred on September 19, 1862 \u2014 the **Battle of Iuka** \u2014 resulting in 1,200 to 1,500 killed or wounded.\n\n- Iuka is located in **northeast Mississippi**. U.S. Route 72 runs through the southern part of the city from west to east.\n\n- The climate is characterized by relatively high temperatures and evenly distributed precipitation throughout the year, classified as a **humid subtropical climate** (K\u00f6ppen \"Cfa\").\n\nWould you like to know more about Iuka, Mississippi \u2014 its history, attractions, or something else?",
